   "population": "loggers",
   "story": "Dunmore Timber ran six log trucks out of this depot at the end of the haul road: a block-walled truck shop with two tall bays and an inspection pit, a parts room and a welding shop under a mezzanine where the dispatcher kept her office, the scale house on its weighbridge, a fuel island and the log deck. The day the Cordon closed the roads, Vera Lindqvist called every truck in. Four came back. The soldiers at the bridge turned Cole around at gunpoint, and the crews sheltered here on cots over the shop, living on the vending machine and Hank's diesel. Benny had brought Dutch down off the ridge with the cough. When Dutch went down in the shop, Hank and the kid put him in the pit and pulled the planks over him; that night Hank went down after him with a light and his key ring and never came up. Vera locked herself in the dispatch office with the payroll safe and the radio, and kept calling trucks four and six on the company channel long after the boys upstairs had stopped coughing. Ray's last load is still on the scale.",
